## 🚀 Quick Start & Installation

### Prerequisites
- Node.js >= 18.x
- Python >= 3.11
- Docker & Docker Compose (Optional)

### Option 1: Running with Docker Compose (Recommended)

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/cv-optimeter-ai.git
cd cv-optimeter-ai

# Copy environment variables
cp .env.example .env

# Start full stack
docker-compose up -d --build
```
Access the application at `http://localhost:3000` and API docs at `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/docs`.

### Option 2: Running Locally for Development

#### 1. Backend Setup
```bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv
# On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate | On Linux/macOS: source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

#### 2. Frontend Setup
```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

---

## 📖 API Documentation

FastAPI automatically generates interactive Swagger & ReDoc documentation:
- **Swagger UI:** `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/docs`
- **OpenAPI Schema:** `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/openapi.json`

### Key Endpoints
- `POST /api/v1/cv/upload` - Upload & parse PDF/DOCX document
- `POST /api/v1/ats/analyze` - Calculate 0-100 ATS Score & diagnostics
- `POST /api/v1/ai/rewrite-bullet` - STAR bullet point rewriting
- `POST /api/v1/ats/match-job` - Job Description vs Resume comparison
- `POST /api/v1/cover-letter/generate` - Generate tailored cover letter
- `POST /api/v1/linkedin/optimize` - Generate LinkedIn headlines & summary

---

## ⚙️ Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and configure key options:

```ini
PROJECT_NAME="CV Optimeter AI"
SECRET_KEY="your-super-secret-key"

# Optional: Add OpenAI Key for LLM rewriting.
# If omitted, system seamlessly uses local NLP engine.
OPENAI_API_KEY=""
OPENAI_MODEL="gpt-4o"

# Database
DATABASE_URL="postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:password@localhost:5432/cv_optimeter_db"
REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379/0"
```

